<title>PAKISTAN: Pakistani bourse shut on local religious holiday.</title>
<headline>Pakistani bourse shut on local religious holiday.</headline>
<dateline>KARACHI, Pakistan 1997-06-26</dateline>
<text>
<p>Pakistan's main bourse, the Karachi Stock Exchange (KSE) will remain closed on Thursday due to a local religious holiday, a KSE spokesman said.</p>
<p>On Wednesday, the Karachi 100-index closed 2.03 points, or 0.13 percent, down at 1,579.49 with 185 losers and 91 gainers. Pak Telecom  fell 0.20 to 31.</p>
<p>						    Wednesday   June 24</p>
<p> KSE all-share index			  1,063.26    1,065.64</p>
<p>Market capitalisation in billion rupees  494.80 495.90Trading value in billion rupees 0.742 1.18</p>
<p>($1 = 40.49 rupees) -- Ibrahim Khan 9221-5685192</p>
